d "q-124611" :question/id #uuid "9c8002d8-e0b3-5c8f-88f0-b9c94fad04ff" :question/math-academy-id "q-124611" :question/is-example false :question/problem "The point $A$ is located in the first quadrant and lies on the unit circle. The $y$-coordinate of $A$ is $\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{3}.$ What is the $x$-coordinate of $A?$" :question/worked-solution "Since the point $A$ lies on the unit circle, it must satisfy the Pythagorean theorem: \n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=1\n$$\n\nSubstituting $y=\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{3}$ into the above and solving for $x$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2} & =1 \\\\ {x}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{3})}^{2} & =1 \\\\ {x}^{2}+(\\frac{5}{9}) & =1 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =1-\\frac{5}{9} \\\\ {x}^{2} & =\\frac{4}{9} \\\\ x & =\\sqrt{\\frac{4}{9}} \\\\ x & =\\pm \\frac{2}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $A$ lies in the first quadrant, $x$ must be positive, so we select the positive answer. Therefore, our final answer is $x=\\frac{2}{3}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-124611/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "87c18ea8-af12-52bd-8420-ec24ed63de65"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-124611"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-65031/selection/ca043a936588db6d866b4986f40da61ea3e2619c1a5b1384da646dd7a6000553" :answer/id #uuid "5c5e91f9-3f04-500d-8571-ff14b7a7dae4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\frac{\\sqrt{21}}{25}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-65031/selection/644691b86d7ac43ed5b6f24dae9b5b39aca7f074badee5f2d113fe3cfbd75819" :answer/id #uuid "8846ac25-79b5-546c-a805-fec06d551902" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\frac{\\sqrt{21}}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-65031/selection/23e07eafcebfec73ae55ea46c043853e549775e4d4820e9dc65d79e183484bdc" :answer/id #uuid "d4f797f8-5333-5654-8009-a4504ed3bcb9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\frac{21}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-65031/se