ourse_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13931905/assets/fc291f1fc5c4a712d3eef7ea2872de621855669d97445b24a2bc7a9da55949d9.png)\n\nAny point $(x,y)$ on the unit circle is related to the central angle $\\theta $ as follows:\n\n$$\nx=cos⁡\\theta ,\\,y=sin⁡\\theta \n$$\n\nWe're given that $y=\\frac{3}{5}$ at the point $P.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\nsin⁡\\theta =\\frac{3}{5}.\n$$\n\nWe can use the Pythagorean identity to find $cos⁡\\theta :$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta +{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta  & =1 \\\\ {cos}^{2}⁡\\theta  & =1-{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta  \\\\ cos⁡\\theta  & =\\pm \\sqrt{1-{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $sin⁡\\theta =\\frac{3}{5}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}cos⁡\\theta  & =\\pm \\sqrt{1-{(\\frac{3}{5})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{1-\\frac{9}{25}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{16}{25}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{4}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe select the positive answer since $cos⁡\\theta $ is positive in the first quadrant. So, $cos⁡\\theta =\\frac{4}{5}.$\n\nFinally, knowing that $tan⁡\\theta =\\frac{sin⁡\\theta }{cos⁡\\theta },$ we have\n\n$$\ntan⁡\\theta =\\frac{(\\frac{3}{5})}{(\\frac{4}{5})}=\\frac{3}{4}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-65072/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "74d05ad6-7e4a-5c50-92d1-ca4b2f00cbb1"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-65072"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-65075/selection/fea7f6b22e69e29a9716f674d580a63eca4b26e1b4ae5c4f38b3026c28b2b97d" :answer/id #uuid "e143bc21-e4b9-5775-be89-e4bdc36f2781" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{9}{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-65075/selection/39b572231dcf40940a24641876ce13f1db3b7aac4a376d8c40f97819bcfbe7ae" :answer/id #uuid "0b0ceb33-bd4e-56f6-b55b-e2fe36cdbaef" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{17}}{9}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-65075/selection/d25d16cdc6cdab1acb4afc5bf83c552718